<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petar Krešimir IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1074</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petar Krešimir IV was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1058 to 1074, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trpimirovic-dynasty">Trpimirović dynasty</a>. He brought the Byzantine towns and islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> under his rule and styled himself king of Croatia and Dalmatia. A supporter of the reforming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>, he founded monasteries, and the town of Šibenik is traditionally linked with him as 'Krešimir's city'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petar-kresimir-iv.jpg" alt="Petar Krešimir IV" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kresimir%27s_seal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
